i.MX6SoloX Blaze: take the FEC1 reference clock from the pad

imx6sx_enet_clk_sel() clears both the FEC clock mux select and the pad
direction unconditionally at machine init. That is right for the RGMII
reference designs, where the PHY has its own crystal, and wrong for an RMII
board where the PHY supplies the 50 MHz reference back to the SoC -- GPR1[13]
has to select the external clock.

This is the whole fix. Nothing needs to set IMX6SX_CLK_ENET_REF: with bit 13
set the reference arrives on the pad, so the SoC's internal ENET_REF is not
the source and its rate does not matter. Confirmed on hardware -- the link
comes up at 100/full with no rate assignment in the device tree at all.

Because it runs at machine init it also overwrites whatever the bootloader
configured, so this cannot be worked around from the device tree or from
U-Boot. The two in-tree i.MX6SX RMII boards, udoo-neo and
softing-vining-2000, carry no clock configuration at all and appear never to
have been exercised against this.

Without it the PHY never answers MDIO, and the failure is not benign: the
FEC's phy-connect error path corrupts the slab, and the kernel oopses in
kmem_cache_alloc about five seconds later in whatever allocates next.

This sets it unconditionally, which is enough to test the theory on one
machine. The upstream shape would key it on the FEC's phy-mode.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/arch/arm/mach-imx/mach-imx6sx.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-imx/mach-imx6sx.c
@@ -20,8 +20,17 @@
 
 	gpr = syscon_regmap_lookup_by_compatible("fsl,imx6sx-iomuxc-gpr");
 	if (!IS_ERR(gpr)) {
+		/*
+		 * FEC1 here is RMII with the PHY driving the 50 MHz reference
+		 * back into the SoC, so GPR1[13] has to select the external
+		 * clock. Upstream hardcodes both fields to zero, which is
+		 * correct only for the RGMII reference designs -- and it
+		 * overwrites whatever the bootloader set, so an RMII board
+		 * cannot work around it from the device tree either.
+		 */
 		regmap_update_bits(gpr, IOMUXC_GPR1,
-				   IMX6SX_GPR1_FEC_CLOCK_MUX_SEL_MASK, 0);
+				   IMX6SX_GPR1_FEC_CLOCK_MUX_SEL_MASK,
+				   0x1 << 13);
 		regmap_update_bits(gpr, IOMUXC_GPR1,
 				   IMX6SX_GPR1_FEC_CLOCK_PAD_DIR_MASK, 0);
 	} else {
